2. SOUND PACK GRANT

   Tread Lightly exists to load third-party sounds. Nothing in Section 1 is
   intended to restrict that, and this section grants the rights needed to do
   it.

   "Sound Pack" means a Minecraft resource pack, or any equivalent collection
   of data and assets (block maps, acoustic definitions, other JSON
   configuration, audio files, and similar), that is loaded at runtime by
   Tread Lightly and does not include any part of the Software's compiled code.

   You are granted a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable right to:

   (a) Create Sound Packs for Tread Lightly, for any purpose, including
       commercial purposes.

   (b) Distribute, sell, and license your Sound Packs on any terms you choose,
       through any channel.

   (c) Use Tread Lightly's pack formats, JSON schemas, field names, directory
       layouts, resource namespace, and the vocabularies it defines for
       substrates, acoustics, states, and events, for the purpose of authoring,
       loading, or interoperating with Sound Packs.

   (d) Copy and modify the configuration files the Software ships, and
       distribute the result as part of a Sound Pack. Authoring a pack normally
       starts from the shipped block map rather than from an empty file, and
       this is permitted.

   (e) Override, replace, or extend any of the Software's own resources from
       within a Sound Pack, including files under the Software's resource
       namespace, using the ordinary Minecraft resource pack mechanism.

   (f) Write separate mods, tools, editors, validators, or libraries that
       interoperate with Tread Lightly through its public API or pack formats.

   You own your Sound Pack. This license claims no ownership over, and imposes
   no licensing terms on, content you create. Loading your work through Tread
   Lightly does not make it a derivative work of the Software, and no
   attribution to Tread Lightly is required.

   This grant is irrevocable: it cannot be withdrawn from Sound Packs already
   published, and it survives any future change to this license.


3. LIMITS OF THE GRANT

   Section 2 does not permit you to:

   (a) Redistribute the Software's own code or binaries, whether modified or
       unmodified, except as allowed in Section 4.

   (b) Republish audio original to this project as a standalone sound library,
       or as the substance of a pack that adds nothing of its own.

       This applies only to audio original to Tread Lightly. Any audio the
       Software ships that comes from Presence Footsteps is under the MIT
       License, and this paragraph does not restrict it; see NOTICE.

       For the avoidance of doubt, this does not restrict a Sound Pack that
       references the Software's shipped sounds by name, nor one that supplies
       its own audio for some sounds and leaves the rest to the Software. A
       pack does not have to avoid the shipped sounds to stay within this
       license.

   (c) Present a Sound Pack in a way that implies it is Tread Lightly itself,
       or that it is endorsed by or affiliated with the project.


4. MODPACK INCLUSION

   You may include Tread Lightly in a modpack, free or paid, provided that all
   of the following hold:

   (a) The modpack uses a distribution format that fetches Tread Lightly from
       an official distribution page operated or authorised by the copyright
       holder. The end user's launcher performs the download; the modpack
       itself carries a reference, not the file. CurseForge manifests and
       Modrinth .mrpack index entries are the intended examples.

   (b) The modpack does not bundle, mirror, re-host, or otherwise include a
       copy of the Tread Lightly JAR.

   (c) Tread Lightly is distributed unmodified. You may not patch, repackage,
       strip, recompile, or alter the JAR in any way.

   (d) Configuration files and Sound Packs shipped alongside are unaffected by
       this section and remain governed by Section 2.

   This permission is automatically revoked for any modpack that breaches (a)
   through (c).


